     1,
     "<p>Dear list,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sorry if this appears twice, I am not sure I managed to crack posting to the group first time around!</p><p>I am having a spot of bother with some plotting. I have\r\ndownloaded the Natural Earth Administrative boundaries and am able to  plot them nicely enough using some of the\r\nmany helpful guides available on the internet. However, one of the default\r\nfeatures in ggplot2 is that it adds a little space to the end of each axis (I\r\nguess to make sure data at the extremes of the axes are plotted ok). I would\r\nlike to remove this excess space so that my polygons go right to the edge of\r\nthe plot area. I can more or less accomplish this by specifying scale limits\r\nwith the expand argument for the x and y scales, e.g.\r\nscale_x_continuous(limits=c(4,8),expand=c(0,0)). However when I do this the\r\nrenderer inexplicably slices off parts of my polygons close to the plot border.\r\nPlay with the limits in the scale_x_continuous() or scale_y_continuous in the\r\ncode below and you will get a good idea of what I mean. Am I doing something\r\nwrong?<br></p><p><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Many thanks for any help,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Simon<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>---<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Below is my session info and a (hopefully) reproducible\r\nexample:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><u></u> <u></u></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">#Load relevant pacakges</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">library(ggplot2)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">library(maptools)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">library(rgeos)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">library(plyr)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">#<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Download and unzip the Natural Earth Country Polygon data</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">oldwd &lt;- getwd()</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">tmp &lt;- tempdir()</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">setwd(tmp)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">url &lt;- &quot;<a href=\"http://www.naturalearthdata.com/http//www.naturalearthdata.com/download/50m/cultural/50m-admin-0-countries.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.naturalearthdata.com/http//www.naturalearthdata.com/download/50m/cultural/50m-admin-0-countries.zip&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375460024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3R49JmzRVT7MxM0-rPMAqx\">http://www.naturalearthdata.com/http//www.naturalearthdata.com/download/50m/cultural/50m-admin-0-countries.zip</a>&quot;</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">dest &lt;- paste(tmp,&quot;\\\\tmp.zip&quot;,sep=&quot;&quot;)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">download.file(url,dest)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>#File is 1.3Mb</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">unzip(dest)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">#<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Read in the data to a SpatialPolygonsDataFrame and subset to West African countries</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">wld &lt;- readShapePoly(&quot;ne_50m_admin_0_countries&quot;)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">wa &lt;- wld[c(21,22,43,44,81,82,84,144,151,158,160,190,195,213),]</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">#<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Convert to data.frame for plotting with ggplot2</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">wa@data$id &lt;- rownames(wa@data) # Explicitly identifies attribute rows by the .dbf offset</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">wa.df &lt;- as.data.frame(wa)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">gpclibPermit() # required for fortify method if rgeos is unavailable</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">wa.fort &lt;- fortify(wa, region=&quot;id&quot;)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><a href=\"http://wa.gg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wa.gg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375460024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ezGE9P7yclAGzRBNIF8MX\">wa.gg</a> &lt;- join(wa.fort, wa.df,by=&quot;id&quot;)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br></blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">#<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Create the plot</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">p &lt;- ggplot(<a href=\"http://wa.gg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wa.gg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792375460024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ezGE9P7yclAGzRBNIF8MX\">wa.gg</a>)+</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>geom_polygon(aes(long,lat,group=group))+</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>geom_path(colour=&quot;white&quot;,aes(long,lat,group=group),size=1.2)+</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>coord_equal()+</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>scale_x_continuous(name=expression(paste(&quot;Longitude (&quot;,degree,&quot;)&quot;)),limits=c(-18,4),expand=c(0,0))+</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>scale_y_continuous(name=expression(paste(&quot;Latitude (&quot;,degree,&quot;)&quot;)),limits=c(4,17),expand=c(0,0))</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">print(p)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">unlink(tmp,recursive=T)</blockquote><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\">setwd(oldwd)</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<p><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p>And my session info:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>----<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>sessionInfo()<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>R version 2.15.0 (2012-03-30)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Platform: x86_64-pc-mingw32/x64 (64-bit)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>locale:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[1] LC_COLLATE=English_United Kingdom.1252 <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[2] LC_CTYPE=English_United Kingdom.1252   <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[3] LC_MONETARY=English_United Kingdom.1252<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[4] LC_NUMERIC=C                           <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[5] LC_TIME=English_United Kingdom.1252    <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>attached base packages:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[1] stats     graphics \r\ngrDevices utils     datasets  methods  \r\nbase     <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>other attached packages:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[1] gpclib_1.5-1   \r\nrgeos_0.2-6     plyr_1.7.1      stringr_0.6    <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[5] maptools_0.8-14 lattice_0.20-6  sp_0.9-99       foreign_0.8-49 <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>[9] ggplot2_0.9.1  <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p>loaded via a namespace (and not attached):<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p> [1]\r\ncolorspace_1.1-1   dichromat_1.2-4    digest_0.5.2       grid_2.15.0       <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p> [5]\r\nlabeling_0.1       MASS_7.3-17        memoise_0.1        munsell_0.3       <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p> [9]\r\nproto_0.3-9.2      RColorBrewer_1.0-5\r\nreshape2_1.2.1     scales_0.2.1<u></u><u></u></p>"
